{title: 078 - For God So Loved Us}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #078 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 78}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
For God so loved us,
He sent the Savior:
For God so loved us,
and loves me too.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
Love so unending!
I'll sing His praises,
God loves His children,
loves even me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He sent the Savior,
the blest Redeemer;
He sent the Savior
to set me free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
He bade me welcome,
O word of mercy;
He bade me welcome,
O voice divine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Glory and honor,
O Love eternal,
To Him be given
while life shall last.
{end_of_verse}
